# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Crab Quest" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Drinking from bottle
1	select	Start Crab Quest?
1	option	Yes.
2	box	Against your better judgement, you pick up the bottle and take a sip...
2	box	...and immediately black out.
2	line	Player	Urrrrrgh!
2	line	Player	I feel like I've just been kicked off Entrana.
2	line	Player	Hey there, little guy! Aww, look at you! You're so cute!
2	line	Crab	No, I'm not.
2	line	Player	Aaaaaaaaaah! You can talk!
2	line	Crab	Of course I can! I'm ugly, not stupid.
2	line	Player	Wait, what? You're not ugly! You're adorable! What makes you think you're ugly?
2	line	Crab	...
2	line	Crab	I stand corrected. I am here getting therapy from a huge fleshy thing I just found on the beach, which quite frankly I should have run from. I must also be stupid.
2	line	Player	Hey now, you shouldn't be so harsh on yourself. Even dubious decisions can turn out well. For instance, I just drank from this random bottle I found, which sounds like a terrible idea.
2	line	Player	And, to be honest, feels like a terrible idea too. Urgh. I now have a pounding headache...
2	line	Crab	I'm still waiting for the bit where this wasn't a terrible idea.
2	line	Player	I got to meet you!
2	line	Crab	I'm STILL waiting for the bit where this wasn't a terrible idea.
2	line	Crab	Hang on, if you thought it was going to be such a terrible idea, why did you even do it?
2	line	Player	I felt... strangely compelled to? It's hard to explain. I just had the conviction that I needed to do it, no matter the consequences.
2	cond	If the player has NPC attack options enabled:
3	line	Player	It happens sometimes... I feel the urge to do something daft, like attacking someone I wanted to talk to. Sometimes I can resist it, and sometimes I can't.
3	action	continues
2	cond	If the player has NPC attack options disabled:
3	line	Player	It happens sometimes... I feel the urge to do something daft, like running in the complete opposite direction to where I wanted to go. Sometimes I can resist it, and sometimes I can't.
3	action	continues
2	line	Crab	Something tells me that I shouldn't take advice from you.
2	line	Player	Sure, I make mistakes, but learning from mistakes makes you wiser!
2	line	Crab	Are you learning, though? Because I am learning nothing from this.
2	line	Crab	Listen, you can rest here for a little while, but we'll be needing the beach back very soon for the ceremony.
2	line	Player	The ceremony? What ceremony?
2	line	Crab	You're not from around here, are you? Very well, then, I will explain.
2	line	Crab	Every year, my kin comes down from the heights and gathers on the beach. There, we perform the ceremonial dance and build sand nests to try and find a mate.
2	line	Player	Wait... Is this literally a dating site?
2	line	Crab	...
2	line	Crab	Yes. And every...
2	box	The crab painstakingly counts up to 16 on his claws.
2	line	Crab	100 years, the turnout is significantly bigger. Legends say that they're echoes of a time where our population boomed. One of those ceremonies will happen in a couple of days.
2	line	Player	Sounds like it's going to be quite the party!
2	line	Crab	Yeah...
2	line	Player	You don't sound convinced.
2	line	Crab	Let's say I've not had a good experience in the past. I... don't really want to talk about it.
2	line	Crab	If only I could be a ceremonial leader, then maybe...
2	line	Player	A ceremonial leader? What do they do?
2	line	Crab	Ceremonial leaders are the ones performing the ceremonial rhythm. Without them, the dance isn't synchronised and the ceremony descends into chaos.
2	line	Crab	That usually results in some crabs complaining loudly about how much they paid to be there.
2	line	Player	Wait... You have to pay to attend?
2	line	Crab	For the most part, no, but if you want to avoid any risk of being trampled, there are sections of the beach which are more exclusive. Personally, I think being mildly trampled is part of the experience.
2	line	Player	I see. Anyhow, why do you wish to become a ceremonial leader?
2	line	Crab	Ceremonial leaders are respected and looked up to as long as they lead the ceremony successfully. It's not usually my thing to stand in front of others, but maybe that's what it takes.
2	line	Player	What it takes for what?
2	line	Crab	To finally be seen...
2	box	The crab's voice trails off as he looks up towards the trees and his face, somehow, appears to turn redder.
2	line	Player	Er... How does one become a ceremonial leader, then?
2	line	Crab	You need an instrument. Usually either seashell or coconut, but good seashells can be hard to find.
2	line	Crab	Say... Even though you only have 2 legs, they're pretty long. You could probably walk around the island and find good shells in no time!
2	line	Player	I suppose. How many do we need?
2	line	Crab	As many different ones as you can find. Bring them here and I'll try them out.
2	line	Player	Okay, then! I'll be back.
2	line	Crab	See ya!
2	action	end
1	option	No.
2	box	You decide against drinking from the bottle after all.
2	action	end
