1	action	end
0	section	Fourth correct shell
1	line	Crab	Cheers! We've got 10 different notes. That beats the last ceremony, but we can do better still.
1	line	Player	Wait, what do you mean, 10? We just had 3 with the last shell I brought!
1	line	Crab	Yes? That's how counting goes! 1, 2, 3, 10.
1	box	The crab points at each finger on his claws in turn.
1	line	Player	Do you know what...? Never mind!
1	action	end
0	section	Fifth correct shell
1	line	Crab	Oh, very nice! We now have... 11 notes. A couple more might be enough.
1	action	end
0	section	Sixth correct shell
1	line	Crab	Thank you! We've almost got enough to make a tune. One more?
1	action	end
0	section	Last correct shell
1	line	Crab	Oh no... I can't easily play 13 different shells on my own, but if I only play one... I won't stand out enough for her to see me!
1	line	Player	Her?
1	line	Crab	Never mind! Every other ceremonial leader will use either seashells or coconuts. Maybe I'd stand out more if I played something else...
1	line	Player	Mmm. Can you blow air?
1	line	Crab	I can blow bubbles.
1	line	Player	I don't think that counts. We can't have a wind instrument. We don't want a percussive instrument. How about a string instrument?
1	line	Crab	A what now?
1	line	Player	A string instrument. The string vibrates and makes a sound.
1	line	Crab	Sounds cool! I want to try one.
1	cond	If the player has a regular lyre in their inventory:
