1	box	The crab squints, then clicks its claws frantically.
1	line	Player	What's this? Has Timmy fallen down the old well?
1	box	The crab scowls, then clicks its claws some more.
1	line	Crab	Cliiick-cliiick-click click cliiick. Click-cliiick-click-click cliiick- cliiick-cliiick click-click-click cliiick.
1	line	Player	That's some pretty deft clawwork you've got there. Have you ever thought of playing shell? I think you have what it takes.
1	line	Crab	Cliiick-click cliiick-cliiick-cliiick.
1	line	Player	Sounds like you agree! So you'll do it?
1	box	The crab viciously attacks your foot.
1	line	Player	You want to shake hands! Awww.
1	box	The crab despondently throws its claws in the air, then scutters away to join the practice.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the crab at practise
1	box	The crab viciously attacks your foot.
1	line	Player	Awww. Sorry little buddy, but I can't be an instrument for the band! You have a lovely shell right there, however!
1	action	end
0	section	Investigating the palm directly east of the western-most palm
1	box	A crab appears!
1	line	Crab	Earthquake! Earthquake!
1	line	Player	No, no, it's okay! I'm here on behalf of my crab friend on the beach.
1	line	Crab	Talking earthquake!
1	line	Player	Would you please listen to me?
1	line	Crab	Angry talking earthquake!
1	line	Player	Fine. The angry talking earthquake bids you to become a ceremonial leader this year. Do my bidding, or else!
1	line	Crab	As you wish, as you wish! Please do not destroy my home!
1	line	Player	Head to the beach to collect your shell.
1	line	Crab	As you wish! Although I prefer playing coconut...
1	line	Player	Then head to the beach to collect your coconut! Do not anger me again!
1	box	The crab scutters away to practise.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the crab at practise
1	line	Crab	Oh no, the angry talking earthquake is back!
1	line	Player	Yes, and I tell you to keep practising!
1	line	Crab	As you wish, as you wish!
1	action	end
0	section	Investigating the palm directly north-east of the western-most palm
1	box	A crab appears!
1	line	Player	Hello! I'm here on behalf of my crab friend on the beach.
1	line	Crab	Oh! Is he cute?
1	line	Player	I think he's adorable, but then I think you all are. No, I'm here because he was looking for crabs to become ceremonial leaders.
1	line	Crab	Shame, girls can't be ceremonial leaders. Although I think it's stupid and we should be able to be leaders if we wanted. It's ridiculous.
1	line	Player	I can't see why you wouldn't be allowed to be a leader. Why don't you go and have a go, and if you being a girl is a problem, let me know. I'll talk to them.
1	line	Crab	Wow, you're pretty cool, whatever you are!
1	box	The crab scutters away to practise.
0	section	Talking to the crab at practise
1	cond	If the crab playing coconut is not present:
2	line	Crab	This is fun!
2	line	Player	Good to hear!
2	action	end
1	cond	If the crab playing coconut is present:
2	line	Player	See, girl! I told you girls could be ceremonial leaders!
2	line	Crab	I'm so glad you did! I am having so much fun! I should do this every year!
2	line	Crab	Also, the crab playing coconut next to me is super cute! I'm so glad I came.
2	action	end
1	line	Crab	While you were away, I heard of a commotion near the northernmost tree on the island. Could you please check it out?
1	line	Player	I didn't notice anything, but I will go and check.
1	action	end
0	section	Investigating the northern-most palm
1	box	A 'crab' appears!
1	line	Player	I'm here on behalf of my crab friend on the... Hey, wait a minute! You're not a crab. You're a penguin!
1	line	'Crab'	My cover has been blown! Unless you are also an agent in disguise? What's the passphrase?
1	line	Player	No, you've been caught red-handed. Come clean, now, what are you doing here!
1	line	'Crab'	The details of my mission must remain a secret. You can't make me talk.
1	line	Player	This island is covered in crabs. I am sure I could find a way to get that info out of you.
1	line	'Crab'	I'll talk, I'll talk! I've been sent on a mission to find food supplies for my homeland. I discovered that an upcoming ceremony will convince many crabs to come out of hiding.
1	line	Player	You want to eat the crabs? I won't let you. Now you better scram or I'm going to make you regret coming here.
1	line	'Crab'	My mission must be successful!
1	line	Player	Likewise!
1	box	A crab appears!
1	line	Crab	Yo! The angry bird... Did it go?
1	line	Player	I kicked him out. We can't have him disrupt the ceremony, now, can we?
1	line	Crab	That's so rad! I was afraid I'd have to miss out! I've been practising my moves all year, it would have been so off beat to miss out. I've been trialling a shell spin that's going to turn heads!
1	line	Player	That sounds amazing! Does that mean I can't convince you to become a ceremonial leader this year?
1	line	Crab	Yo, now I didn't say that! Being a leader is an even bigger honour than being a dancer. You're one with the beat. I couldn't pass that up!
1	line	Player	Excellent! Then if you could head down to the beach, you'll find what you need to practise!
1	box	The crab scutters away to practise.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the crab at practice
1	line	Crab	Yo! This tune is going to be so good, I'm going to regret not being able to dance it.
1	line	Player	I would have loved to see it!
1	line	Crab	Heh! My shell spin doesn't work on dry sand anyway! I know, I tried!
1	action	end
0	section	Returning to the main crab before finding the main crab's crush
1	line	Crab	We could do with, er, more girl leaders.
1	line	Player	I will try and ask your crush to join.
1	line	Crab	What? No! You are not going to do that because I'm not going to admit to having a crush and you can't make me.
1	line	Player	Hmm-mmm! I got you!
1	action	end
0	section	Investigating the palm directly north of the magic tree
1	box	A crab comes out shyly.
1	line	Player	Hey there! I'm looking for ceremonial leaders to help my friend on the beach.
1	line	Crab	Oh. Sorry. You've come to the wrong crab!
1	line	Player	How comes?
1	line	Crab	First, I'm a girl and girls are never ceremonial leaders. Besides, I get very nervous standing in front of others... I'm afraid to mess up.
1	line	Player	What if you do? Messing up is a part of life. You fall and pick yourself back up again.
1	line	Crab	I know that, and yet I can't help it. I have this uneasy feeling that I don't belong... But I just really want to be accepted.
1	line	Player	I hear you.
1	line	Crab	If only I could be more like...
1	box	The crab appears to turn bright red.
1	line	Crab	You see, there's this one crab... He's kind and funny... and handsome! When he's around I feel like everything is going to be okay. But unfortunately, I can't even look at him!
1	line	Player	Why not?
1	line	Crab	For a start. I... get all red. In fact I get all red just thinking about him!
1	line	Crab	It's really confusing how he makes me feel at ease yet so nervous at the same time. If I was a ceremonial leader and I spotted him... I would mess up for sure.
1	line	Crab	No, the only way I can ever look at him is to steal some side glances...
1	line	Player	Wait. Since you walk sideways, which way IS a side glance?
1	line	Crab	The way I'm walking! Which means if I try to walk towards him, I can't even look where I'm going!
1	line	Crab	So I look at him from afar when he doesn't know I'm around. Yet among a thousand crabs on the beach, he's the only one I see.
1	line	Player	Awww. I don't know which crab is the one that caught your eye, but you obviously like him. Hey, maybe he's a ceremonial leader this year?
1	line	Crab	I already can't handle how awesome he is. If he was a ceremonial leader as well, how could I possibly approach him? I already can't!
1	line	Player	I clearly can't convince you to join, but the leaders will be practising on the beach if you wanted to check in advance whether the crab of your dreams will be playing.
1	line	Player	And if he is, that might be your chance! Who knows! Maybe 'that crab you can't look at' only wants one thing: for you to look at him!
1	line	Crab	Very unlikely! But maybe I will take a peek. The good thing about being pessimistic is that you're happy when you're wrong!
1	box	The crab scutters away.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the crab next to the chest
1	line	Player	I take it from your colour that he's around?
1	line	Crab	Yes, and he seems to be playing an instrument I've never seen before! He is SO cool!
1	cond	If the player said the instrument was a disaster:
2	line	Player	Ah, yes, the Disaster.
2	line	Crab	Hey, take that back, he's not a disaster!
2	line	Player	No no no! I don't mean he's a disaster. That's the name of the instrument I made for him!
2	line	Crab	You made him an instrument called a disaster?
2	line	Player	I was only owning to the fact that it wasn't my best work, but the name stuck...
2	action	continue
1	cond	If the player said the instrument was a bass:
2	line	Player	Ah, yes, the bass.
2	line	Crab	That's not a bass! A bass is a type of fish! Also, what's with that accent?
2	line	Player	Believe it or not, that's exactly what he said.
2	action	continue
1	cond	If the player said they did not know the name of the instrument:
2	line	Player	Ah, yes, the Banjo. He named it himself.
2	line	Crab	Wow! Is there anything he cannot do?
2	line	Player	Actually, yes. He can't play more than one note yet. It's just a matter of time, though!
2	action	continue
1	line	Crab	You know? I feel bad spying on him like this. I wish I could just walk to him and find out how he feels about me.
1	line	Player	What's stopping you?
1	line	Crab	I am afraid of him not liking me, of course. But I might be even more afraid of him actually liking me!
1	line	Crab	What if I'm... I don't know... not right for him? What if I end up hurting him one day?
1	line	Player	He might have an opinion on that. You two are going to have to figure this out. Together.
1	line	Crab	I can't even approach him, let alone talk to him! And yet when I do manage to look at him... He feels like home, like where I ought to be. It's so confusing!
1	line	Player	Go to him once the ceremony has ended. If he spots you and blushes, then you've got nothing to lose. You've got this!
1	action	end
0	section	Investigating the north-western most tree
1	box	No crab is coming out of the tree. Maybe they are too scared?
1	action	end
0	section	Sitting by the tree
1	box	And now, you wait...
1	box	A crab appears!
1	line	Player	Hello! My friend on the beach is looking for crabs to become ceremonial leaders.
1	line	Crab	...
1	line	Player	Are you okay?
1	line	Crab	I... just want to retract my eyes and feel saltwater wash all over me. Taking me back to a time when I was a child and things were simple. Where the weight of life didn't feel so... heavy.
1	line	Crab	I feel so trapped. I feel like I am about to moult, but the shell won't break. My thoughts are too big for me. I long to be tossed by the waves, helpless. Feel nature's wrath. Feel alive.
1	line	Player	That's deep. It sounds like being part of a community, making new friends and doing something meaningful could be really good for you. Be a ceremonial leader this year.
1	line	Player	Practice is on the beach. What do you have to lose? Besides, the sea will only be a scuttle away if it doesn't work out.
1	cond	If the player has talked to the crab nicknamed "Dipper":
2	line	Player	Although the last crab that did that has been nicknamed Dipper ever since.
1	line	Crab	... Alright.
1	box	The crab scutters away to practise.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the crab at practise
1	line	Player	Hey, how are you doing?
1	line	Crab	Better. Playing coconut is tiring work, but it's kind of liberating. The sound drowns my thoughts.
1	cond	If the crab at the red shell is present:
2	line	Crab	My lovely neighbour is also really kind to me. She seems to care for me more than I can fathom.
2	line	Crab	Aw, shush! You looked like you were carrying the weight of a coconut. That's not right.
2	line	Crab	Your liveliness is making my day so much brighter, my load so much lighter. Who needs the sea when the sun is warmer?
2	line	Crab	Awwww. He's a keeper!
2	action	end
1	action	end
0	section	Investigating the north-eastern most tree
1	box	No crab is coming out of the tree. Maybe they are too scared?
1	action	end
0	section	Sitting by the tree
1	box	And now, you wait...
1	box	A crab appears!
1	line	Player	Hello! I'm here on behalf of my crab friend on the beach who is looking for crabs to become ceremonial leaders.
1	line	Crab	My, my, what do we have here? I have never seen one of your kin before.
1	line	Player	No? There are ruins on this island that look like they were made by my kind.
1	line	Crab	Truly? Are you one of the ancient ones, whose tales have been passed downs for thousands of generations?
1	line	Player	Noooo? Maybe?
1	line	Crab	Oh, what a great scientific discovery! Would you object to answering a few questions?
1	line	Player	I... er...
1	box	The crab pokes at your foot.
1	line	Crab	So fascinating! Your carapace here seems to be very different from that of your upper limbs. Can I take a few measurements?
1	box	The crab starts measuring your foot with its claw.
1	line	Player	Listen... I just want to help my friend down on the beach. Are you willing to help?
1	line	Crab	And miss out on the scientific discovery of the century! No, I must take notes.
1	box	The crab starts sketching on the bark of his tree.
1	line	Player	Okay, then I'll be heading off.
1	line	Crab	So soon? Would you mind if I tagged along? For science?
1	line	Player	What will you take notes on if you leave the tree behind?
1	line	Crab	That is... very astute! I must note that down. Oh, before you go, can I have a carapace sample?
1	line	Player	No!
1	action	end
0	section	Investigating the plant
1	box	A crab appears!
1	line	Crab	Aaaaah! No! I'm too old to die!
1	line	Player	Do not be afraid!
1	line	Crab	Being afraid has saved my chitin more than once, so I'll be afraid whether you like it or not!
1	line	Player	Er... Anyway, I'm here on behalf of my crab friend down on the beach. He is looking for ceremonial leaders to join him and his new instrument.
1	line	Crab	Oh! Well, I'll pass as I'm not going. The ceremony is not worth the hassle.
1	line	Player	How so?
1	line	Crab	You spend ages travelling out to end up on a noisy overcrowded beach, crammed with crabs who climb all over you and don't respect you at all, you can't see anything, it's cold, and there's sand everywhere!
1	line	Crab	And then when it's all over, you have to travel all the way back. You're exhausted and you wish you hadn't left home. I hate it. But you do it for the kids, right?
1	line	Player	Right?
1	line	Crab	Right! Not that you ever know which ones your kids are. We don't stick around to find out!
1	line	Player	Er...
1	line	Crab	For all I know, you could be my kid.
1	cond	If the player has already talked to the magic tree crab:
2	line	Player	I sincerely doubt that. Actually, talking to another crab, I was under the impression that lineage was very important to crabs.
2	line	Crab	Only for some! These stuck-ups aristocrabs once got lucky enough to get their claws on the magic tree, and now they think they are a gift to crabdom.
2	line	Crab	Passing it down through generations. Exclusive ceremony beach corners. Pah! Anything to feel superior.
2	line	Crab	All it means is that they get to act like the rest of us are inferior. Yet I bet to seagulls, we all taste the same.
2	action	continues
1	cond	If the player hasn't already talked to the magic tree crab:
2	line	Player	I sincerely doubt that.
2	action	continues
1	line	Crab	Anyway, I just want a year off from the ceremony. It's not too much to ask! I hear it's going to be even more crowded this year. Nobody will mind if I skip.
1	line	Player	Do ceremonial leaders get trampled too?
1	line	Crab	No, they usually stay on the heights. We can't risk having the ceremonial rhythm be disrupted.
1	line	Player	So you would perform quite close to home?
1	line	Crab	I suppose I would. But the practice takes place on the beach, doesn't it? It'd be a lot of effort to get back.
1	line	Player	What if I carried you back up once you're done practising? Would you consider it?
1	line	Crab	Hrm. Okay then, you've convinced me. I'll help.
1	box	The crab scutters away to practise.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the crab at practise
1	cond	First time if the crab on the red shell is present:
2	line	Player	See, girl! I told you girls could be ceremonial leaders!
2	line	Crab	You told me no such thing, and I am not a girl. She is, however.
2	line	Player	I can't tell you apart. That's really embarrassing.
2	action	end
1	cond	Subsequent times or if the crab on the red shell isn't present:
2	line	Crab	After all this, I still had to trek all the way to the beach.
2	line	Player	But at least you're not getting trampled?
2	line	Crab	That is a small mercy.
2	action	end
0	section	Investigating the western bush
1	box	The crab stares past you serenely.
1	line	Player	Hello! I'm here on behalf of my crab friend over there. He's looking for crabs to become ceremonial leaders.
1	line	Crab	The circle of life must continue.
1	line	Player	It must, yes. And so I wanted to know if you would be interested in joining? Practice is taking place... Right there.
1	line	Crab	As the swallow carries the coconut, the body must toil.
1	line	Player	Does that mean you'll join?
1	line	Crab	The path to enlightenment forgoes distractions.
1	line	Player	Does that mean you won't join?
1	line	Crab	A life not lived is a mind not opened.
1	line	Player	Does that mean...? Oh I give up.
1	box	The crab serenely scutters away to practise.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the crab at practise
1	line	Player	How are you doing?
1	line	Crab	The mind is quiet, the coconut is not.
1	action	end
0	section	Investigating the eastern bush
1	box	A crab appears!
1	box	The crab clicks its claws threateningly.
1	line	Player	Hey there! I'm not here to fight. I'm here on behalf of my crab friend over there.
1	line	Crab	Speak.
1	line	Player	He is looking for ceremonial leaders to join him and make a cracking tune. He has a cool new instrument to use and good-sounding shells to share.
1	line	Crab	Oh! Then I hope the ceremonial music will be better than last year. That time, the drums sent me into a trance and I walked right into the ocean instead of doing the dance. It was awful.
1	line	Player	...
1	line	Crab	I've been building amazing nests year after year and nobody cared. I went for a dip ONCE and now everyone calls me Dipper.
1	line	Player	Maybe becoming a ceremonial leader will help them forget about that? And you'd be too busy playing to accidentally go for a dip again.
1	line	Crab	...
1	line	Crab	It's worth a shot. Okay, I will do it.
1	box	The crab scutters away to practise.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the crab at practise
1	line	Player	Hey there! How's it going?
1	line	Crab	Well, I've not earned a new nickname since starting practice. We'll see how that works out.
1	action	end
0	section	After finding all six leaders to join practise
1	line	Player	Unless I really like talking to crabs, I've probably found enough leaders. I could go back to see how the practise is going.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the main crab
1	line	Player	How is the practice going?
1	line	Crab	Pretty good! We've got enough leaders to practice properly. There's room for more, of course, but I expect if we don't look for them, they will come by themselves.
1	line	Crab	It's up to you! You can continue talking to my kin and recruiting leaders or you can wait for them to turn up.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Look for more leaders.
2	line	Player	Any idea where to look?
2	line	Crab	I would check next to bushes and trees. You may find some of us hiding in some. We crabs can be scared of tall things which are not trees.
2	line	Crab	If you struggle to make contact, you may want to make yourself flatter to the ground.
2	line	Player	Got it!
2	action	end
1	option	Wait for leaders to turn up.
2	line	Player	I've done enough talking. I'll wait here.
2	action	continues
0	section	After finding every crab to join practise
1	line	Player	I think I have found all of the crabs that were going to be leaders. I should go back to see how the practice is going.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the main crab
1	cond	If every crab has joined practice:
2	line	Player	I'm afraid I've found all the crabs that were willing to assist.
2	line	Crab	Oh. To be fair, that is probably for the best. I don't think I have the nerves for the alternative.
2	line	Player	Is there a certain crab you wanted to be a ceremonial leader that isn't here?
2	line	Crab	That's none of your business!
2	line	Crab	Anyway, the whole band is complete! Thanks for your help.
2	action	continues
1	cond	If not every crab has joined practice:
2	line	Crab	The whole band is complete! Thanks for your help.
2	action	continues
1	line	Crab	I don't have much to offer in return, but maybe I could show you the ceremonial dance of my kin? Just promise me you won't do it during the ceremony.
1	line	Player	Why? Are you afraid I will become irresistible to a certain someone?
1	line	Crab	No, I'm afraid you'll trample us.
1	line	Player	Hey!
1	line	Crab	I'm not sure how well this is going to work given you only have 2 legs.
1	line	Player	Only one way to find out!
1	line	Crab	Let's go over there where it's a bit less crowded.
1	action	continues
0	section	Crab rave
1	line	Crab	The point of the dance is to make a sturdy sand nest.
1	line	Player	That's definitely a skill I need to level up.
1	line	Crab	You can sway and wave your claws in time with the music if you want to...
1	cond	If the player has unlocked the Crab dance emote:
2	action	continues
1	cond	If the player has not unlocked the Crab dance emote:
2	action	continues
1	line	Crab	But to be honest, the only thing that really matters...
1	line	Crab	Is what your back legs are doing.
1	line	Player	I don't have back legs! Unless I put one at the front and one at the back, like this?
1	line	Crab	Use those legs to move the sand and gently and push it away.
1	line	Player	I will just use one.
1	line	Crab	As you slowly turn around on the spot...
1	cond	If the player has unlocked the Crab dance emote:
2	line	Crab	Buddy, what are you doing?
2	line	Player	Swaying and waving my claws?
2	line	Crab	Look, honestly, I don't think it's working out. Got any other moves?
2	line	Player	Awww... Okay, how's that?
2	line	Crab	Better!
2	action	continues
1	line	Crab	You can change direction once you've done a full rotation.
1	line	'Crab'	Mission?
1	line	Player	Oh no you don't!
1	line	Crab	What?
1	line	Player	Nothing!
1	line	Player	Am I doing this right?
1	line	Crab	Not really.
1	line	Player	We are just drawing a circle.
1	line	Crab	That's how it starts.
1	line	Crab	But if you do it long enough, you have a nest.
1	line	Player	I bet I can do it faster! Watch this!
1	line	Player	Noooooooooooooo! Lil' guy!
1	line	Player	What have I done!
1	line	Player	I should have listened to you!
1	line	Crab	Disputable.
1	line	Player	You're alive!
1	line	Crab	Somehow, yes. But anyways, we are done here. Thank you for coming to my demonstration.
1	line	Crab	Please never attempt this again.
1	action	continues
